# Agent Self-Evaluation (mandatory)

**Every agent turn that responds to the user MUST end with a `### Self-evaluation` block.** No exceptions — including read-only Q&A, single-line answers, Ask mode, and failed/aborted work.

Full process: `.cursor/skills/agent-self-evaluation/SKILL.md`

## Hard requirements

1. **Run before sending the final message** — not optional, not deferred to a follow-up.
2. **Include `### Files used`** then **`### Self-evaluation`** as the **last sections** of the response (files in **load order**).
3. **Context load audit** — every turn: correct files, no excess load, proper order (classify before deep read), **[AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) not stale** (update it when routing drifts); kanban cards: use **Label Methods** before broad grep when Feature Areas are set.
4. **§6 skill & rule feedback loop** — every turn: mental check (both §6 questions).
   **Read-only / Ask:** no file writes unless urgent; handoff one line each —
   `Skills updated: none (read-only)` / `Rules updated: none (read-only)`.
   **Implementation / fix / refactor:** edit **≥1 skill + ≥1 rule**; handoff names both — not
   `none`. **Anti-bloat:** grep + consolidate-before-expand per SKILL §6c/§6d — Signature:
   `governance-compact-self-eval-handoff`. Structured forward feedback (six categories) runs **only**
   on Card Done — Signature: `card-done-forward-feedback`
   ([kanban-markdown/SKILL.md](../skills/kanban-markdown/SKILL.md) § Card Done); Card Done turns
   also surface top 3 items in chat (`### Top forward feedback` before handoff — SKILL §7).
5. **§6g consistency** — when this turn edited [agent-consistency.mdc](../rules/agent-consistency.mdc) `globs`, run [SKILL.md](../skills/agent-self-evaluation/SKILL.md) §6g before handoff; list drift alert lines or `KNOWN_DRIFT:` when parity not fixed; else N/A.
6. **Drift alerts in handoff** — governance-edit turns with unresolved parity: include `- **Drift alerts:**` (`[info|warn|critical]` + prefix line, or `KNOWN_DRIFT:` per reference § KNOWN_DRIFT); else `none (N/A)`.
7. **Failure patterns** — on failure signals at task start, grep per [agent-triage/SKILL.md](../skills/agent-triage/SKILL.md) §1b; on end-of-turn churn, grep [reference.md](../skills/agent-self-evaluation/reference.md) § Common failure patterns. Cite **Signature** in rule edits — do not duplicate **Fix pattern** prose.
8. **Never skip** because the task was "trivial", "docs-only", "question-only", or "no code changed" (implementation still requires both updates).
9. **Ruff E501 before handoff** — implementation turns that edit `.py`/`.pyi`: run
   `.venv/bin/ruff check --select E501` on touched paths before the final message — Signature:
   `ruff-e501-line-length` ([pre-commit-workflow/SKILL.md](../skills/pre-commit-workflow/SKILL.md)).

## Handoff block (required format)

Canonical compact template: [SKILL.md](../skills/agent-self-evaluation/SKILL.md) §7 — Signature:
`governance-compact-self-eval-handoff`. Required every turn: `### Files used` then
`### Self-evaluation` (one line per field). **Do not** duplicate the full template here.

## Pair with agent-triage

Start every task with [agent-triage](../skills/agent-triage/SKILL.md). **Repo index:** [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md). End every task with self-evaluation. A response without the handoff block is **incomplete**.
